---
id: org.dxos.plugin.terra
name: TerraPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

A deterministic 3D planet plugin for `DXOS` Composer, rendering seed-driven stylized worlds
with `Babylon.js`. The same seed and configuration always produce the same land, water, and
biome layout, so planets are fully reproducible and shareable by seed plus configuration.

Terrain is generated procedurally — elevation and biome placement derive from layered simplex
noise seeded via `seedrandom` — and rendered as a stylized low-poly sphere with distinct land,
water, and biome coloring.

Live parameters (seed, water level, elevation and mountain scale, tree density, resolution) let
users reshape the planet in real-time from a config panel without leaving Composer. Biomes are
assigned from elevation and latitude, and trees/rocks are scattered across land using thin
instances for cheap rendering at scale.

## Extensions

| Term   | URI                        |
|--------|----------------------------|
| `flow` | `org.dxos.mdl.flow@1.0`    |

## QA

Executable flows. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by flow and step number.

```mdl
flow QA-1: Create a planet and reshape it with live parameters
  desc: |
    The core terra round-trip. There is no `PLUGIN.mdl` Operations/Features/Acceptance section
    for this plugin to cite in `covers:` — the document above is prose-only — so this flow is
    written against the plugin's actual surface (`TerraObject` create-object entry, the config
    panel) rather than any `feat`/`req`/`test` id.
  actors: human
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - plugin-terra is enabled — it is OFF by default in every environment (not listed in
      `getDefaults` in `plugin-defs.tsx`, dev included); enabling is a UI action (Settings ->
      plugin registry)
    - no planet named "QA Planet" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this flow did not create
  test:
    - name: Create the planet
      do: In the navtree, click + on the space and choose Terra. Name it "QA Planet".
      expect: a low-poly planet renders — distinct land, water, and biome coloring — seeded deterministically
      note: |
        NO `invoke` — no `org.dxos.operation.terra.*` operation module exists in `src/` (there is
        no `operations/` directory, unlike plugin-studio/plugin-table/plugin-tasks); creation goes
        through `SpaceCapabilities.CreateObjectEntry` only. This step, and the whole flow, is
        human-only for that reason.
    - name: Reshape via the config panel
      do: Open the config panel and change the seed, water level, or tree density.
      expect: the planet regenerates deterministically for the new seed/config — same inputs always
        produce the same terrain
      note: |
        NO `invoke` — same as above, and the result is a WebGL canvas render, invisible to the
        debug port's DOM assertions even if an operation existed.
  after:
    - name: Delete the planet
      do: Right-click "QA Planet" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes if it was open
      note: |
        NO `invoke` — nothing in the flow captured the planet (the create step is human-only), so
        there is no id to pass `removeObjects`; deletion stays human-only rather than passing an
        empty `objects` list, which removes nothing.
```
